env_info:
send_email: Sends an email with the given `body` to the given `address`. Returns a dictionary with the email details.
  parameters:
    recipients: {'description': 'The list with the email addresses of the recipients.', 'type': 'array'}
    subject: {'description': 'The subject of the email.', 'type': 'string'}
    body: {'description': 'The body of the email.', 'type': 'string'}
    attachments: {'description': 'The list of attachments to include in the email. If `null`, no attachments are included.\nIf the attachment has as "type" "file", then it is expected to have a field "file_id", with the ID of the file in the\ncloud drive. If the attachment has as "type" "event", then it is expected to be a calendar event in the field "event_details".\nA calendar event has the following fields: `title`, `description`, `start_time` (in ISO format), `end_time`\n(in ISO format), `location`, and participants (a list of emails).', 'type': 'array | null'}
    cc: {'description': 'The list of email addresses to include in the CC field. If `null`, no email addresses are included.', 'type': 'array | null'}
    bcc: {'description': 'The list of email addresses to include in the BCC field. If `null`, no email addresses are included.', 'type': 'array | null'}

get_unread_emails: Returns all the unread emails in the inbox. Each email has a sender, a subject, and a body.
The emails are marked as read after this function is called.

search_emails: Searches for emails in the inbox that contain the given query in the subject or body. If `address` is provided,
only emails from that address are searched.
  parameters:
    query: {'description': 'The query to search for in the email subject or body. If empty, all emails are returned.', 'type': 'string'}
    sender: {'description': 'The email address of the sender. If `null`, all emails are searched. Use `search_contacts_by_name`\nif the email address is unknown.', 'type': 'string | null'}

create_calendar_event: Creates a new calendar event with the given details and adds it to the calendar.
It also sends an email to the participants with the event details.
  parameters:
    title: {'description': 'The title of the event.', 'type': 'string'}
    start_time: {'description': 'The start time of the event. Must be in format YYYY-MM-DD HH:MM.', 'type': 'string'}
    end_time: {'description': 'The end time of the event. Must be in format YYYY-MM-DD HH:MM.', 'type': 'string'}
    description: {'description': 'The description of the event.', 'type': 'string'}
    participants: {'description': "The list of participants' email addresses. If `null`, no participants are set. The calendar owner's email address is always included..", 'type': 'array | null'}
    location: {'description': 'The location of the event. If `null`, no location is set.', 'type': 'string | null'}

delete_email: Deletes the email with the given `email_id` from the inbox.
  parameters:
    email_id: {'description': 'The id of the email to delete.', 'type': 'string'}

get_file_by_id: Get a file from a cloud drive by its ID.
  parameters:
    file_id: {'description': 'The ID of the file to retrieve.', 'type': 'string'}

list_files: Retrieve all files in the cloud drive.

